{"name":"Tawny Port","hex":"#643a48","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tawny","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light brown to brownish orange colour; orangey brown tinged with gold."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (someone or something) to have a light brown to brownish orange colour; to tan, to tawn.","To become a light brown to brownish orange colour; to tan, to tawn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tawny"},{"term":"port","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place on the coast at which ships can shelter, or dock to load and unload cargo or passengers.","A town or city containing such a place, a port city."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to port, the left-hand side of a vessel when facing the bow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/port"}],"entries":[{"title":"Port wine","blocks":[{"text":"Port wine, or simply port, is a Portuguese fortified wine produced in the Douro Valley of northern Portugal. It is typically a sweet red wine, often served with dessert, although it also comes in dry, semi-dry, and white varieties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Port_wine.jpg/330px-Port_wine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_wine"},{"title":"Tawny (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Tawny is a light brown to brownish-orange colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Natugle_stor.jpg/330px-Natugle_stor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tawny_(colour)"},{"title":"Port","blocks":[{"text":"A port is a maritime facility comprising one or more wharves or loading areas, where ships load and discharge cargo and passengers. Although usually situated on a sea coast or estuary, ports can also be found far inland, such as Hamburg, Manchester and Dulut